      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_dbde4075",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: wing_wing_wing; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a man in a suit on a phone call, with the text \"wing wing wing\" overlaid. The text is likely meant to mimic the sound of a bird or a playful, nonsensical phrase. The overall intent is not inherently abusive, hateful, or propagandistic, but the phrase \"wing wing wing\" could be interpreted as a childish or mocking sound effect, potentially used to imply absurdity or silliness. While not targeting any specific group with harmful stereotypes, the meme's intent is to create humor through juxtaposition — the serious, professional appearance of the man contrasted with the childish, nonsensical text. This could be seen as mildly harmful if it is used to mock someone's speech or behavior in a derogatory way, but without context, it is primarily a harmless, humorous meme. The image does not contain any explicit toxic elements such as racism, sexism, ableism, or other forms of discrimination. The intent is to evoke amusement through absurdity, not to attack or harm any group or individual.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
